#{[17592186174952 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186174953] [17592186174958 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186174961] [17592186174970 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186174973] [17592186175414 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186175416] [17592186175420 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186175424] [17592186176355 :question/worked-solution "Cosine has period $2\\pi$ and is even. Therefore $\\cos(-x+16\\pi)=\\cos(-x)=\\cos x=-11/24$."] [17592186176466 :question/worked-solution "The model has solution $P(t)=P_0e^{rt}$. Doubling after ten years gives $e^{10r}=2$, so $r=\\ln2/10$. For tripling,\n$$\ne^{rt}=3,\\qquad t=\\frac{\\ln3}{r}=\\frac{10\\ln3}{\\ln2}\\approx15.8496.\n$$\nIt took **15.8 years**, to one decimal place."] [17592186176467 :question/worked-solution "The model has solution $T(t)=T_0e^{-rt}$. Reducing **by** four-fifths leaves one-fifth, so $e^{-2r}=1/5$ and $r=\\ln5/2$. Reducing to one-fifteenth requires\n$$\ne^{-rt}=\\frac1{15},\\qquad t=\\frac{\\ln15}{r}=\\frac{2\\ln15}{\\ln5}\\approx3.3652.\n$$\nThe required time is **3.4 minutes**, to one decimal place."] [17592186176468 :question/worked-solution "For $P'=-0.1P$, populations four years apart satisfy\n$$\nP(9)=P(5)e^{-0.1(9-5)}=3200e^{-0.4}\\approx2145.024.\n$$\nThus the model predicts approximately **2145 penguins**, to the nearest whole penguin."] [17592186176469 :question/worked-solution "The model is $P(t)=P_0e^{0.09t}$. At $t=18$,\n$$\n8000=P_0e^{1.62},\\qquad P_0=8000e^{-1.62}\\approx1583.190.\n$$\nThe initial population was approximately **1583 fish**, to the nearest whole fish."] [17592186176470 :question/worked-solution "With $P(0)=150000$, the solution is $P(t)=150000e^{0.055t}$. Set $P(t)=400000$ and solve:\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\ln(400000/150000)}{0.055}\\approx17.8333.\n$$\nRounded to the nearest year, the answer is **18 years**."] [17592186176472 :question/worked-solution "With $N(0)=150000$, the solution is $N(t)=150000e^{-0.05t}$. Reaching $50000$ particles requires\n$$\ne^{-0.05t}=\\frac13,\\qquad t=\\frac{\\ln3}{0.05}\\approx21.9722.\n$$\nRounded to the nearest year, this is **22 years**."] [17592186176546 :question/worked-solution "Cosine has period $2\\pi$, so $\\cos(x-6\\pi)=\\cos x$. Hence $4\\cos(x-6\\pi)-1=4(\\sqrt3/2)-1=2\\sqrt3-1$."] [17592186176547 :question/worked-solution "The shift $10\\pi$ is five full periods, so $\\cos(x+10\\pi)=\\cos x=-1/\\sqrt3$."] [17592186177219 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177220] [17592186177225 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177228] [17592186177231 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177233] [17592186178143 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186178145] [17592186178149 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186178153] [17592186179925 :question/worked-solution "At one half-life $H$, $e^{-0.53319H}=1/2$. Thus $H=\\ln2/0.53319=1.3000\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{s}$, which rounds to $1.3\\,\\mathrm{s}$."] [17592186179926 :question/worked-solution "Exponential decay gives $M(t)=M_0\\,2^{-t/H}$. At the stated time, $t/H=1.5$, so $M=100\\,2^{-1.5}=35.3553\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{pg}$, or $35.36\\,\\mathrm{pg}$."] [17592186179927 :question/worked-solution "The remaining fraction is $0.15=2^{-t/717000}$. Taking logarithms gives $t=717000\\ln(1/0.15)/\\ln2=1962404\\ldots$ years, approximately $1$ million $962$ thousand years."] [17592186180079 :question/worked-solution "The remaining fraction is $6.25/200=1/32=(1/2)^5$. Five half-lives have elapsed, so $t=5(15.2)=76\\,\\mathrm{s}$."] [17592186180080 :question/worked-solution "At the half-life, $e^{-0.001k}=1/2$. Therefore $k=\\ln2/0.001=693.147\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$, which is $693$ to three significant figures."] [17592186180169 :question/worked-solution "The remaining fraction satisfies $0.70=2^{-t/12.3}$. Therefore $t=12.3\\ln(0.70)/\\ln(0.5)=6.3292\\ldots$ years, or $6.3$ years to one decimal place."] [17592186181456 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186181460] [17592186181462 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186181467] [17592186181468 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186181471] [17592186181502 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186181507] [17592186183042 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186183043]}
